## 7. What remains

Generic H6 is not excluded. The current exact outer state has 14174 labelled cells.

The next layer should use the metric angle data now that every surviving cell has both a full generic chirotope and a complete edge-sign assignment. For each cell one can derive the cyclic order of the five signed force rays at all seven non-ground vertices, express each force turn as an affine function of reciprocal radial-angle gaps, and impose simultaneously:

- all Euclidean triangle angle-sum equations for the eight reciprocal points;
- strict positivity and the chirotope half-plane inequalities for radial gaps;
- the five exact turn-simplex inequalities at each of the seven physical pentagons.

A numerical discovery check on an initial sample already finds many of these 14174 cells affine-infeasible, but no numerical result is used in this note. The next rigorous step is to extract exact rational Farkas certificates for that affine system, as was done in the generic `H7b` branch.

Collinear reciprocal triples remain outside this generic branch and must still be handled separately.

No theorem-state file is changed. C-II remains open.
